<title>USA: IBM names Mitisubishi exec to board.</title>
<headline>IBM names Mitisubishi exec to board.</headline>
<dateline>ARMONK, N.Y. 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Business Machines Corp said Tuesday it has expanded the size of its board of directors to 12 members, electing Mitsubishi Corp President Minoru Makihara to fill the new spot.</p>
<p>&quot;Makihara-san is a truly global executive who not only heads one of Japan's most important companies, but also has broad experience and understanding of the global economy and major markets of the world,&quot; IBM Chairman and Chief Executive Louis Gerstner said in a statement. &quot;I have known him for many years.  His experience and interests are broad and he will be a very valuable addition to the IBM board.&quot;</p>
<p>Makihara has been president of Mitsubishi since 1992.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
